# RGB_STATE's truth (module/rgb_state_sim.c): every D7 83 read, parsed as the app does, against
# the fake strip's last frame (what the LEDs show) through idle, wake, the PC's frames (lit while
# ZMK's flag is off; dark while the on/off is on), a breathe at its darkest, and sync off and on;
# the D7 83 event after each change and its lit; then #624: the left's look in the RGB op the
# right is sent, and a right with an older saved look taking it (only what differs); #618: the
# right's ring before the left's first status read keeps its shown block, and as the right the
# LEDs go dark with the left's idle while the PC's traffic runs, lit again on a left key.
/^rgbstate:/p
s/.*hid_listener_keycode/kp/p
